From 98b43ff9db829016e61f7aec3c7829df88ce96c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marek Blaha <mblaha@redhat.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 05:50:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] repo: suppress transient "Signing key not found" error from
 progress bar
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When a repository has repo_gpgcheck=1 and the signing key hasn't been
imported yet, the progress bar showed a confusing error message
"repomd.xml GPG signature verification error: Signing key not found"
before the user was prompted to import the key. This error is transient
— it is resolved once the key import succeeds.

Suppress the error from the download callbacks only during the first
download pass when key import will be attempted (import_keys is true).
On the second pass (after key import was attempted/refused), the flag is
false and the error is shown normally.

Extract is_signing_key_not_found_error() helper into repo_pgp to
share the string matching between the callback suppression and the
existing handle_repo_exception() check.

Includes two tests:
- test_load_repo_gpgcheck_no_keyring_error: when the user accepts
  key import, no "Signing key not found" error is reported via
  download callbacks (suppressed on the first pass, resolved on
  the second).
- test_load_repo_gpgcheck_refused_key_shows_error: when the user
  refuses key import, the error is reported exactly once (suppressed
  on the first pass, shown on the second pass when suppression is
  off).

https://github.com/rpm-software-management/dnf5/issues/2810

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Marek Blaha <mblaha@redhat.com>
---
